# NetMifi Pro — AI Code Generation Rules

Hackathon Next.js app. Features built here are intended to land in `netmifi-mono` later.
Match mono quality (types, Biome, portable UI) without copying the monorepo layout.

## Project Identity

- **App**: Next.js App Router (not Vite / TanStack Router)
- **Runtime / package manager**: Bun (`bun install`, `bun run`, `bun test`)
- **Formatter / linter**: Biome (`biome.json`)
- **UI**: React 19 + Tailwind CSS 4
- **Imports**: `@/` path alias (see `tsconfig.json`)

This is a single Next.js app, not a Bun workspace. Do not invent `apps/*` or `@netmifi/*` packages here.

## Next.js

- Treat this Next.js version as different from older docs. Prefer `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` over training data.
- App Router only (`app/`). No Pages Router.
- Default to Server Components. Add `"use client"` only when the component needs state, effects, or browser APIs.
- Do not use deprecated Next.js APIs.

## Code Style

- Biome: double quotes, semicolons always, tabs (width 2), line width 100, trailing commas ES5
- Prefer `interface` for object shapes; `type` for unions, intersections, and computed types
- Never use `any` — use a real type, generics, `unknown`, or `never`
- Prefer `??` over `||` for null/undefined defaults
- Sort Tailwind classes: layout → spacing → typography → colors → effects
- JSDoc on utility functions (`@param`, `@returns`, `@throws` when relevant)
- Comment why, not what, in non-obvious or security-sensitive code

## File Organization

```
app/            routes, layouts, loading/error UI (Next.js only)
components/     presentational UI (keep free of Next/data fetching)
lib/            env, utils, server-only helpers, data access
public/         static assets
```

- Co-locate route-only UI under `app/` when it is not reusable
- Put reusable UI in `components/` so it can move to `@netmifi/design` later
- Put shared logic in `lib/` so it can move to `@netmifi/utils` / `@netmifi/env` later

## Portability (later → netmifi-mono)

- Presentational components: props in, JSX out — no `next/navigation`, no `next/link` inside reusable UI (pass `href` / callbacks / slots from `app/`)
- No data fetching inside reusable components
- Do not couple business logic to Hono, tRPC, or TanStack Router here unless the hackathon requires it
- Env: centralize in `lib/env.ts` when secrets/config appear; never scatter `process.env`
- Client env vars must use `NEXT_PUBLIC_`
- Prefer libraries already used in mono when a dependency is needed (zod, date-fns, better-auth, drizzle)

## TypeScript

- Strict mode; `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` is on
- `import type` for type-only imports
- Type guards over assertions (`as`)

## When Generating Code

1. Follow Biome (double quotes, semicolons, tabs)
2. Never use `any`
3. Keep `components/` portable; keep Next.js APIs in `app/`
4. Handle loading, empty, and error states
5. Prefer `??` over `||` for nullish defaults
6. Sort Tailwind classes
7. Use Bun, not npm/yarn/pnpm
8. Do not import from `netmifi-mono` until we explicitly wire a workspace dependency
